```bash
node index.js
```

5. In your Discord server, open the Developer Portal and create a new application. Under the "Bot" tab, click "Add Bot" and copy the generated token.

6. In the Discord Developer Portal, navigate to the "Bot" tab and click "Add Slash Command". Fill in the required fields with the following information:

- Command Name: `ban`
- Description: `Bans a user from the server`

7. Click "Create" to create the slash command.

8. Under the "Bot" tab, click "Bot" > "Reset Token". Copy the new token generated.

9. In your terminal, stop the bot with `Ctrl+C`.

10. Run the following command to update the bot's token:

```bash
node index.js --token=YOUR_NEW_DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN_HERE
```

11. In your Discord server, use the `/ban` command followed by a user's tag (e.g. `/ban @user#1234`) to test the bot's functionality.

Note: This implementation assumes that you have already set up the necessary permissions for the bot to ban users in your Discord server. Make sure to grant the bot the necessary permissions in your server's settings.

